    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483-a2">

                <pb facs="0565" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg485"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Molloy to Mr. Naphen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brighton, Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-01-14"><hi rendition="#italic">January 14,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In regard to my brother, who is an English
                    prisoner of war on Morgans Island, Bermuda, I have just been in conversation
                    with Mr. Tearney, a young man who was with my brother in South Africa. He
                    received a letter from him yesterday, informing him that he was sick in the
                    prison hospital. He also informs me that my brother was very anxious to come
                    home with the rest of the corps the time they came, but that he was forced to
                    join the Boer artillery or be shot. The letter that Mr. Tearney received from
                    him has come through the British, and I have no reason to doubt but it is true.
                    Hoping that you will use your valuable influence, and thanking you sincerely for
                    what you have already done toward his release,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hugh B. Molloy.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
